-- title:
--   Lemma 3.8: the extreme generated algebra is simple tube type
-- statement:
--   All Lie algebras below are real and finite-dimensional, with their usual Hausdorff vector-space topology; brackets of subspaces denote real linear spans. Let $\mathfrak g$ be hermitian simple. Let $h\in\mathfrak g$ have semisimple adjoint, with complex spectrum contained in $\{0,\pm\frac12,\pm1\}$, and suppose both $\mathfrak g_{-1}(h)$ and $\mathfrak g_1(h)$ are nonzero. Then the Lie algebra generated by these extremes has the independent internal sum
--
--   $$\mathfrak g_t(h)=\mathfrak g_{-1}(h)\oplus[\mathfrak g_{-1}(h),\mathfrak g_1(h)]\oplus\mathfrak g_1(h),$$
--
--   and is hermitian simple of tube type. Spectral containment does not require every listed value to occur. This is a structural statement used in the paper's classification of causal subalgebras.
-- source:
--   Classification of 3-graded causal subalgebras of real simple Lie algebras, arXiv:2001.03125v2, PDF p. 21, Lemma 3.8

